@meta
id: 06-15
title: Comma takes you back
chapter: 06
type: lesson
skills: repeat-semicolon, find-f, line-start
par: 37
minutes: 5
vscode: four clicks and a lot of squinting
open: customers.csv

@brief
Two rows of a customer export. The company name field contains spaces, so
whatever reads this file next needs it quoted:

    ord_1042,cus_88,"Watford Retail Ltd",4999,GBP,CANCELLED

A quote goes on each side of the third field. The closing quote sits just
before the third comma; the opening quote sits just after the second. Those
are the same target, found in two different directions, and you already know
how to repeat a find — you just need to repeat it backwards.

@keys
| `3f,` | forward to the third comma |
| `;` | repeat the last find, same direction |
| `,` | repeat the last find, opposite direction |
| `i` `a` | insert before, insert after |

@hints
Place the closing quote first, working left to right with a counted `f`.
Then the opening quote is one comma back from where you are standing.
--
`,` repeats your last find in reverse. After a forward `f,` it searches
backwards for a comma, which is exactly one field's worth of travel.
--
`3f,` `i` `"` `Esc`, then `,` `a` `"` `Esc`. Then `j` `0` and the same again
on the second row.

@solution
    3f, i " <Esc> , a " <Esc> j 0 3f, i " <Esc> , a " <Esc> :wq<Enter>

The key to read is the key you already type a hundred times a day as
punctuation, and out of insert mode it means back one. `;` and `,` are a
pair: forward again, back again. Nothing else about the find changes, so you
can overshoot deliberately, notice, and step back for one keystroke rather
than restarting the whole motion.

That is the honest workflow, by the way. Nobody counts commas perfectly
first time. What fluent vim looks like is a slightly wrong jump followed by
a `;` or a `,` — two keys, no thought, no mouse — rather than a perfect jump
every time.

Careful with the direction: `,` reverses the direction of the original find,
so after `F,` it searches forwards. It reverses; it is not a fixed compass.

@start customers.csv
ord_1042,cus_88,Watford Retail Ltd,4999,GBP,CANCELLED
ord_1043,cus_91,Brent Cross Cafe,1250,GBP,PENDING

@expected customers.csv
ord_1042,cus_88,"Watford Retail Ltd",4999,GBP,CANCELLED
ord_1043,cus_91,"Brent Cross Cafe",1250,GBP,PENDING
